{
  "info": {
    "name": "City Complaint & Service Platform API",
    "_postman_id": "b7a6-city-complaint-0001-000000000000",
    "description": "Complete collection for the City Complaint & Service Platform backend.\n\nWorkflow: run **Auth → Login (Admin)** or **Login (Citizen)** first — the test script stores the JWT in `{{token}}`. Most create requests store the new id in a collection variable (categoryId, serviceId, complaintId, serviceRequestId, reviewId, agentId, sessionId, paymentId) so later requests chain automatically.\n\nSuccess responses are `{ success, message, data }` (+ optional `meta`); errors are `{ success, message, errors }`.",
